@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Size-prior comparator locked protocol
+
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`
+
+This protocol was written before the size prior was fitted or its held-out
+metrics were calculated.
+
+- Reuse `scripts/compare_target_parametrisations.py` for its corpus loaders,
+  exact-label audit, split, seed, feature construction, estimator fitting,
+  tie-breaking, and metric definitions.
+- Reuse `.scratch/parametrisation-comparison/tuning.json` without tuning or
+  changing any hyperparameter. Refit the learned additive and interaction
+  heads on the same final train+validation rows used by that comparison.
+- Fit `SIZE_PRIOR` once on those train+validation rows by ordinary least
+  squares against the exact interaction target with coalition size as a
+  categorical variable. Thus each fitted value is the training mean at that
+  integer size. Do not interpolate or regularize.
+- Score the frozen held-out rows as:
+  - `LEARNED_PSI = learned_additive + learned_interaction`
+  - `SIZE_PRIOR = learned_additive + fitted_size_prior`
+  - `ZERO_PSI = learned_additive`
+  - `EXACT_PSI = learned_additive + exact_interaction`
+- Report exactly the requested metrics. For the requested distribution of
+  `LEARNED_PSI` minus `SIZE_PRIOR` scores over all held-out rows, use `n`,
+  mean, population standard deviation, minimum, p05, median, p95, and maximum.
+  Selection ties inherit the configuration-ID tie-break.
+- Define signed regret margins as `LEARNED_PSI - SIZE_PRIOR` and
+  `SIZE_PRIOR - ZERO_PSI`; negative is better for the left-hand scorer.
+- Require the recomputed `LEARNED_PSI` metrics to equal the frozen comparison's
+  `ADDITIVE` metrics to numerical tolerance before emitting the report.
+
